## Source justifications

Substantive claims mapped to the originating issue and implementation changes:

- Bearer handler allocates a token substring: "It sliced the token out of the `Authorization` header with `authorization["Bearer ".Length..]`, which allocates a copy of the whole token (≈730 chars → ≈1.5 KB for a typical Identity access token) only so it can be passed to `ISecureDataFormat.Unprotect(string)`, which immediately Base64Url-decodes it into bytes." (#70218)
- Size of the saving: "**−1.46 KB (−16%) allocated per bearer-authenticated request**" (#70218)
- Internal-only approach: "`BearerTokenConfigureOptions` now creates the default `BearerTokenProtector` as a new internal `BearerTokenTicketDataFormat`, which derives from `TicketDataFormat`" (#70218)
- Standard base64 must keep working: "If the token contains `+` or `/` (i.e. it may be standard Base64, which `Base64UrlTextEncoder.Decode` also accepts), it falls back to the existing string path, so the set of accepted tokens is unchanged." (#70218)
- Failures return null: "returning `null` on any failure exactly like `SecureDataFormat.Unprotect`" (#70218)
- Custom protectors keep the existing path: "Custom protectors and tokens provided via `OnMessageReceived` use the existing code path unchanged." (#70218)
- Built-in formats built on `SecureDataFormat<T>`: "`SecureDataFormat<T>` (used by `TicketDataFormat`, which backs cookie auth, and by `PropertiesDataFormat` for remote auth state) allocates two full-size intermediate arrays on every call" (#70228)
- Span protector available: "The default data protector already implements `ISpanDataProtector`, which Antiforgery and `CookieTempDataProvider` already use." (#70228)
- Protect allocates the protected array and then the string: "`Protect` gets a new protected `byte[]` from `IDataProtector.Protect`, then base64url-encodes it." (#70228)
- Plaintext copy remains: "Then copy the plaintext out once, because `IDataSerializer<T>.Deserialize` takes a `byte[]`." (#70228)
- Standard base64 input accepted by the existing decoder: "`Base64UrlTextEncoder.Decode` also accepts standard base64 with `+`/`/`" (#70228)
- Default implementations calling existing members so the interface change is not breaking: requested by the proposal author in review discussion.
- Raw-token-bytes use case (`ReadOnlySpan<byte>`) and `TryProtect` shape: chosen by the proposal author in review discussion; no in-repo consumer yet.

